{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.no_growth_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.no_growth_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PerBlockWeightFeasibility.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**The class-level statement.** For any two targets whatsoever, both are\nattainable — so no inequality between attained growths can distinguish the\nclass. Corollary of `growth_ratio_attains_any`, recorded as the form the Δ_λ\nargument actually uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.growth_ratio_attains_any","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.growth_ratio_attains_any","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PerBlockWeightFeasibility.lean#L64-L81","doc":"**Every positive A-growth is attainable.** Given any target `t > 0`, there\nare non-negative per-block weights `u` (on the numerator's index set) and `v`\n(on the denominator's) realising it exactly.\n\nThis is what disjointness of the index sets buys: `u` and `v` are unconstrained\nrelative to one another, so the ratio carries no information about the weight.\nHence the per-block-weight class is **not excludable** by any finite list of\nfailed candidates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.sum_pointMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.sum_pointMass","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PerBlockWeightFeasibility.lean#L58-L62","doc":"A point-mass–weighted sum collapses to the single term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.pointMass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.pointMass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PerBlockWeightFeasibility.lean#L51-L55","doc":"A point mass is non-negative when its size is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.pointMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PerBlockWeightFeasibility.pointMass","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PerBlockWeightFeasibility.lean#L47-L48","doc":"A weight concentrated on a single index (a point mass of size `c`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}